  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data and streamlining internal processes. It was introduced with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000. The project has since secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. A budget update increased the initial phase cost to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, and a separate $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training. The executive board later approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing. The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year."
